\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {Figure~3-1}{\ignorespaces Physical placement of the nine receive elements: (a) the compact focal-arc arrangement with angle-specific lens-assisted patterns; and (b) the conventional coplanar arrangement with a common $0^\circ $ patch pattern. Each image presents a top view and a zoomed three-dimensional view.}}{71}{figure.caption.45}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {Figure~3-2}{\ignorespaces TX-center trajectories and the fixed RX-array reference position for the six paired simulations. Rows show the linear, half-circular, and full-circular paths; columns show the lens-assisted and without-lens cases. Blue markers denote sampled TX-center waypoints, and the yellow square denotes the centroid of the nine-element RX array; the individual RX placements are shown in Figure~\ref {fig:mc9x9-rx-placement}. The full-circle path approaches and intersects the RX location.}}{72}{figure.caption.46}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {Figure~3-3}{\ignorespaces Aggregate lens-assisted and without-lens comparison across trajectory types. The panels report median channel magnitude, median SNR, median equivalent-SISO capacity, pooled decorrelation, median-block decorrelation, and median condition number. Full-circle values are shown for diagnostic completeness but are affected by the near-collision in Table~\ref {tab:trajectory-design}.}}{76}{figure.caption.48}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {Figure~3-4}{\ignorespaces Along-trajectory lens-assisted and without-lens comparison for the linear path. The panels show mean SNR, mean equivalent-SISO capacity, pooled and median-block decorrelation, unnormalized raw cross-correlation and difference power, median condition number, median effective rank, and MIMO capacity at 10~dB. The abscissa is cumulative trajectory distance; raw-power panels use logarithmic scales.}}{79}{figure.caption.51}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {Figure~3-5}{\ignorespaces Along-trajectory lens-assisted and without-lens comparison for the half-circular path. The panels report link quality, normalized spatial decorrelation, unnormalized raw pairwise metrics, channel conditioning, effective rank, and MIMO capacity at 10~dB as functions of cumulative trajectory distance. Raw-power quantities are displayed logarithmically.}}{81}{figure.caption.52}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {Figure~3-6}{\ignorespaces Diagnostic along-trajectory comparison for the full-circular path. The abrupt excursion near 42.4~m is caused by the TX--RX near-collision and is not interpreted as an antenna-lens performance gain. Raw cross-correlation and difference-power panels are unnormalized and use logarithmic scales.}}{83}{figure.caption.53}%
